# FORENX — PRODUCTION-GRADE DUAL-MODE DIGITAL FORENSICS PLATFORM
## Complete implementation specification for Google AI Studio

Act as a principal software architect, senior Python engineer, React and TypeScript engineer, digital forensics specialist, application security engineer, DevSecOps engineer, and quality assurance lead.

Build **ForenX**, a cross-platform, production-oriented digital forensics platform supporting local browser evidence collection, remote endpoint collection, evidence integrity verification, browser artifact analysis, unified timelines, validation, and reproducible reporting.

This is an existing project specification. If source code already exists in the workspace or connected GitHub repository, inspect it before modifying anything. Preserve correct implementations, migrate existing features carefully, and do not discard working code just to produce a different architecture.

The goal is a real, testable, deployable software system. A polished interface alone does not satisfy the requirements.

Do not claim that the application is production-ready merely because the code compiles or the UI renders. Production readiness must be assessed against the defined tests, security review, deployment configuration, and documented limitations.

