# 12. PRODUCTION SECURITY AND PRIVACY

Create a documented threat model and security review.

## API security
- HTTPS in production
- Strong user and endpoint authentication
- Strict request schemas
- Rate limiting
- Request-size limits
- Input validation
- Secure error responses
- Secret management
- Dependency security scanning

## Endpoint security
- Only predefined collection jobs
- No arbitrary command execution
- No silent installation
- No hidden persistent agent
- No credential collection
- No unrestricted filesystem collection
- No privilege escalation
- Explicit collection authorization

## Evidence security
- Protected evidence storage
- TLS for remote transfer
- Storage encryption appropriate to the deployment
- Optional encrypted offline packages using a maintained and reviewed encryption format
- Strict access controls
- Evidence retention settings
- Secure cleanup of temporary processing files
- No sensitive content in ordinary logs
- No evidence upload to third-party AI services

Do not implement custom cryptographic algorithms.

## HTML and archive safety
- Escape untrusted HTML content
- Validate archive member paths
- Reject path traversal
- Apply archive size and file-count limits
- Never execute package content
- Safely handle malformed data

## Audit protection
Use append-only audit workflows where practical and consider hash chaining to expose accidental or unauthorized modification. Document that local hash chaining does not prevent a privileged user from replacing all records and recomputing the chain.

## Privacy controls
- Collect the minimum necessary artifacts.
- Display the collection scope.
- Record authorization.
- Support retention and deletion policy workflows.
- Avoid scanning unrelated users or folders.
- Never collect passwords, cookies, or authentication tokens in the initial release.
- Explain what is collected before each acquisition.

